# Task List API — one request per endpoint, in an order you can run top to bottom.
# Works with Visual Studio, Rider and VS Code (REST Client). Start the API first:
#   docker compose up -d db && dotnet run --project src/TaskList.Api
# Named requests (# @name) let later requests reuse ids from earlier responses.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080/api/v1

### Health (outside /api/v1)
GET http://localhost:5080/health/ready

### UC-01 · Create category
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study",
  "description": "Books and courses",
  "color": "#1e90ff"
}

### UC-01 · Create category with a duplicate name (409 Category.NameAlreadyExists)
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "STUDY"
}

### UC-01 · Create a second category (used to move a task)
# @name createOtherCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Work"
}

### UC-02 · Get category by id (with task counters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}

### UC-03 · List categories (paged, search)
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories?page=1&pageSize=20&search=stu

### UC-04 · Update category
PUT {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Study & Courses",
  "description": "Books, courses and talks",
  "color": "#1E90FF"
}

### UC-06 · Create task
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Read the Clean Architecture book",
  "description": "Chapters 1 to 5",
  "categoryId": "{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}",
  "priority": "High",
  "dueDate": "2099-11-15"
}

### UC-06 · Create task with validation errors (400 Validation.Failed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "ab",
  "categoryId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### UC-07 · Get task by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}

### UC-09 · Update task (details + move to another category)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Read the Clean Architecture book",
  "description": "Chapters 1 to 10",
  "categoryId": "{{createOtherCategory.response.body.$.id}}",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "dueDate": "2099-12-01"
}

### UC-10 · Start task (Pending → InProgress)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}/start

### UC-11 · Complete task (→ Done, sets completedAt)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}/complete

### UC-10 · Start a Done task (409 Task.InvalidStatusTransition)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}/start

### UC-12 · Reopen task (Done → Pending, clears completedAt)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}/reopen

### UC-08 · List tasks (filters, sorting, paging)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?status=Pending&priority=Medium&search=clean&sortBy=dueDate&sortDirection=asc&page=1&pageSize=10

### UC-08 · List overdue tasks
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?overdue=true

### UC-14 · List tasks of a category
GET {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{createOtherCategory.response.body.$.id}}/tasks?sortBy=priority&sortDirection=desc

### UC-05 · Delete a category that still has tasks (409 Category.HasTasks)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{createOtherCategory.response.body.$.id}}

### UC-13 · Delete task
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}

### UC-05 · Delete category (now empty)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{createOtherCategory.response.body.$.id}}

### UC-05 · Delete the first category
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/categories/{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}
